in the mid way, which is no good (IF said entry should be at extreme).\n\nAlso, what happen when price break the first of your ZOI? will you take a trade on the retrace to the DP, and TP at your second ZOI (from bottom up)?\n\nSorry to ask a lot of questions at once, because I think it's all tightly related...","a":"kxfx","d":"","n":"#65","p":3,"im":[],"m":65},{"id":"gembel_p3_66","t":"Away\n\nkxfx wrote: Hey bro,\n\nCan I ask what do you mean when you are saying \"watching PA\" at the zone of interest ( let's make it short - ZOI )? is PA an engulf of opposite direction from where price coming from?\n\nSomething like when price getting close/touch/inside the ZOI, you'll want to wait for engulf down (your 4 ZOIs)?\n\nWhat would it need to engulf that counts as a real engulf (Not FO)? breaking/engulfing last flag? There are flags in all LTFs (M1, M5, M15), which one that you would weight more? Very often I saw that an engulf of M1 flag failed to flip price, and engulf of M15 flag has put price too far and entering will be in the mid way, which is no good (IF said entry should be at extreme).\n\nAlso, what happen when price break the first of your ZOI? will you take a trade on the retrace to the DP, and TP at your second ZOI (from bottom up)?\n\nSorry to ask a lot of questions at once, because I think it's all tightly related...\n\nhai mate... you'll want to wait for engulf down (your 4 ZOIs)? ---> no... i will wait for PB.. the question which one do react (ofc sell higher do provide a good R:R)\n\niam not expert enough to identify FO or EG, still working on it.. engulfed FL that hold price will be important my 2 cents..\n\nlately i have fantasy/dream so much","a":"gembel","d":"","n":"#66","p":3,"im":["b33df0ba70da28a0e7603b0a1b5589b63cba512a","be76a4150c824e97b76171ba03feb7aaca76056b"],"m":66},{"id":"gembel_p3_67","t":"Away\n\nucad","a":"gembel","d":"","n":"#67","p":3,"im":["3dd0bd109ec570c47ae6d466a31b5fe56253b908"],"m":67},{"id":"gembel_p3_68","t":"Hi bro,\n\nThanks for your respond. Really appreciate your help on the GU analysis! Btw, what's that \"Key engulfed\" in your chart? From top down, the first key engulfed is an FL? and the second one is an FTR? Please correct me if I'm wrong. If I'm right, why both are \"keys\"?\n\nAlso, can you share me your concept of what is normal engulf and what is key engulf\n\nThe concept of FO is pretty blurry for me too. Still working on it as well. It seems to me that every engulf can be a FO.\n\nThanks anyway!","a":"kxfx","d":"","n":"#68","p":3,"im":[],"m":68},{"id":"gembel_p3_69","t":"Away\n\nGU lol.. missed trade..\n\nucad","a":"gembel","d":"","n":"#69","p":3,"im":["65b5450586e7205735a37d9bc7238034093b4347","9c0e929d17df9f5fa28755d00e95c01c00885ca3"],"m":69},{"id":"gembel_p3_70","t":"Away\n\nGU & UCAD","a":"gembel","d":"","n":"#70","p":3,"im":["65f374dbae1f87c37e8f10543dfd3ba814854d7e"],"m":70},{"id":"gembel_p3_71","t":"Away\n\nucad analysis mistake..","a":"gembel","d":"","n":"#71","p":3,"im":["c41b2789796fce8a0e10b3ca9800e818b971821c"],"m":71},{"id":"gembel_p3_72","t":"Away\n\nGU..","a":"gembel","d":"","n":"#72","p":3,"im":["66f49439758d0c067659c977df384c1d4e1c892e"],"m":72},{"id":"gembel_p3_73","t":"Away\n\ngembel wrote: GU..\n\nanother BE trade..after drop +-26 pips to FL... waiting PA @ bottom for buy opportunity////","a":"gembel","d":"","n":"#73","p":3,"im":["66f49439758d0c067659c977df384c1d4e1c892e","f947001e0876fb7d9cee643c9b779b9f3d8e4da5"],"m":73},{"id":"gembel_p3_74","t":"Away\n\nGU..","a":"gembel","d":"","n":"#74","p":3,"im":["93db8a296f16030a934b33cd813d0dc38a2decbe"],"m":74},{"id":"gembel_p3_75","t":"Away\n\nmapping on EU pair..","a":"gembel","d":"","n":"#75","p":3,"im":["55610d4bcc17ef0e3e4d17b880235cb6d530d87a"],"m":75}],"images":[{"k":"bf27e27da143aad90bd0fd65dd6e563e19bcf176","t":"assets/thumbs/bf27e27da143aad90bd0fd65dd6e563e19bcf176.webp","f":"assets/images/bf27e27da143aad90bd0fd65dd6e563e19bcf176.png","w":1362,"h":614,"b":19246,"o":"bf27e27da143aad90bd0fd65dd6e563e19